  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7b8860589b05b4642ab42b24201a782d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Note_Marigolds
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GrandmasHouse.Data.NoteData
  kind: 0
  title: Marigolds
  recipe: {fileID: 0}
  body: '(stand-in until Grandma''s own note is added)


    Put a marigold right
    in beside each tomato. The hornworms go for the marigolds and leave the tomatoes
    be. If you do find one, just pick it off and give it a toss.


    Pinch off
    the little shoots that come up between the stem and a branch. They only steal
    from the fruit.


    A garden with no flowers in it is just work.'
  marginNote: Save the seed heads in the fall. Paper sack on the pantry shelf.
  pages: []
  mentions: []
